# tests/captures/basic.rxt — [M4.5a] capture-group expectation seed corpus.
#
# Every `m`/`ms` line here is verified the same way the base tier is: the
# whole-match span is checked against the compiled artifact by
# tests/harness/run.sh (and cross-verified against python re by
# verify_rxt.py, same as tests/base/). What's new is the `g`/`gp` lines that
# follow each case — per-GROUP capture-slot expectations, oracle-verified
# against python re's match.span(slot) (see docs/testing.md's "Capture-group
# expectations" section for the full format).
#
# `g <slot> <start> <end>` = LIVE: must be checkable NOW. `gp` = PENDING-VM:
# may be beyond what today's DFA-only artifacts deliver (RX_NCAPS is 1 for
# every pattern before [M4.5]'s VM lands — see match_api_m4.md D42.2), and is
# counted separately rather than run, until RX_NCAPS grows to cover it.
#
# Almost every group slot here is >= 1, i.e. PENDING today by construction —
# that's expected, not a gap: the DFA engine computes the correct overall
# match span (already exercised, unaffected by this file) but does not
# deliver per-group offsets, only the VM does ([M4.5]). A handful of `g 0`
# lines are included deliberately: slot 0 (the whole match) IS deliverable by
# every artifact today (RX_NCAPS >= 1 always, C3), so those are LIVE checks,
# exercising the non-pending path of the same mechanism the pending lines use.

pattern (a)(b)(c)
m "abc" 0 3
g 0 0 3
gp 1 0 1
gp 2 1 2
gp 3 2 3

pattern (foo)?bar
m "bar" 0 3
gp 1 -1 -1

pattern (foo)?bar
m "foobar" 0 6
gp 1 0 3

pattern a(b|c)+d
m "abccbd" 0 6
gp 1 4 5

pattern (\d+)-(\d+)
m "12-345" 0 6
g 0 0 6
gp 1 0 2
gp 2 3 6

pattern ((a)(b))c
m "abc" 0 3
gp 1 0 2
gp 2 0 1
gp 3 1 2

pattern (a)|(b)
m "b" 0 1
gp 1 -1 -1
gp 2 0 1

pattern (a)|(b)
m "a" 0 1
gp 1 0 1
gp 2 -1 -1

pattern (a)*b
m "b" 0 1
gp 1 -1 -1

pattern (a)*b
m "aaab" 0 4
gp 1 2 3

pattern (x)(y)?(z)
m "xz" 0 2
gp 1 0 1
gp 2 -1 -1
gp 3 1 2

pattern (x)(y)?(z)
m "xyz" 0 3
g 0 0 3
gp 1 0 1
gp 2 1 2
gp 3 2 3

pattern (ab|a)(c|bcd)(d*)
m "abcd" 0 4
gp 1 0 2
gp 2 2 3
gp 3 3 4

# startpos integration: g/gp lines attach to `ms` exactly like `m`.
pattern (a+)(b+)
ms 2 "xxaabbyy" 2 6
gp 1 2 4
gp 2 4 6
